h-quality Fabrizio Ward and NYT/Siena surveys", "Prediction markets price Peltola near 70% to win", "Sullivan's incumbency and the state's R+6 lean cut against the polling trend", "Late-September NYT report on Peltola campaign turmoil is a fresh risk"], "rationale": "Recent polls from independent and even Republican-leaning pollsters show Peltola ahead by 3 to 6 points, and markets price her near 70%, offsetting Sullivan's incumbency and Alaska's Republican lean. The consensus of expert raters clusters at Tossup with several calling it a Democratic flip, supporting a modest Peltola edge.", "watch": "Whether the New York Times report on turmoil in Peltola's campaign moves polling over the final weeks, or Sullivan consolidates Republican voters behind him.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Dan Sullivan (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Alaska's Senate race pits incumbent Republican Dan Sullivan against Democrat Mary Peltola, who advanced from the August primary. Polling since then consistently shows Peltola slightly ahead, with independent surveys giving her a 3-to-6-point lead and even Republican-leaning pollsters showing a close race. Prediction markets put her win probability near 70 percent, and several expert raters call the race a Democratic flip, though others keep it a Tossup or Tilt R.\n\nSullivan retains structural advantages: the state leans Republican by about six points and incumbents usually outperform. Peltola has outraised him substantially, but Sullivan holds more cash and faces less outside opposition spending. A late-September New York Times report describing turmoil in Peltola's campaign is the main new variable, and inflation concerns among Alaskan voters keep the race competitive. The forecast gives Peltola a modest edge with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5747, "margin": 0.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6995, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6035, "margin": 2.0}]}